From 2ce4581484b7d69e4b56d6d74488b19a12b24d62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 01:22:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adopt NEON sadalp/smlal reductions + if-convert covered
 loads, csel fusion hardened

Backport of levkropp 36e6cb18, the last substantial commit in his tree.
Adopted: VecSadalpI32x4 4-wide i32->i64 sum reduction (sadalp accumulates
sign-extended pairs, exact for integer sums), VecSmlalLo/HiI32x4 dot
products, the saddlp/uaddlp/sadalp/uadalp encoder fix (size field from
the SOURCE arrangement - was a reserved encoding -> SIGILL), if_convert
covered-arm-load rewriting (copy-chain aware), and AArch64 fused
cmp+csel via the new supports_fused_cmp_select hook.

TWO BUGS IN HIS COMMIT FOUND BY OUR ARM DIFFERENTIAL SUITE AND FIXED:

1. ASSEMBLY FAILURE (huft_build_crash): select_arm_reg emitted
   'mov w2, x0' for 32-bit selects - not a valid A64 form (width must
   match on both sides). Source is now w0 when the scratch is a w-reg.

2. MISCOMPILE (pgo_sections, training output 770104689198169071 !=
   365601466280353968): detect_cmp_select_fusion allowed the Cmp to sit
   ARBITRRARILY far above the Select. The fusion re-emits the Cmp at the
   Select's program point, but in the accumulator-based codegen the
   intervening instructions clobber the scratch registers the Cmp
   operands lived in - pgo_sections' if-chain then compared k-87
   instead of k ('add w8, w8, #-87' reused the register between the
   three sunk compares). Fusion is now restricted to the immediately
   adjacent shapes 'cmp; select' and 'cmp; copy; select', where the
   register state at the re-emit point provably equals the state at the
   original Cmp. CCC_NO_FUSED_CSEL=1 added for A/B bisection.

Merge notes: byte_offset_iv (ours) and second_acc (his) both threaded
through insert_reduction_remainder_loop; our loud unhandled-intrinsic
diagnostic on x86 kept instead of his silent no-op arms; his smlal dot
patterns pass through OUR stricter reduction soundness gate (currently
rejects the multiply shape conservatively - correct result, sadalp sum
path fires and is verified). Task-file edits dropped.

PROOF: sadalp fires on 4096-i32 sum, qemu == gcc (-2048); dot product
correct (-627, scalar); huft + pgo_sections both pass again; ARM
differential 101/25 (baseline held), 166/166 x86, 673 lib, 50/50
correctness, 3/3 intrinsics, 300/300 fuzz; x86 sieve asm BIT-IDENTICAL
to origin/main (all new hooks default-false on x86).
